<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Xoybûn</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1927">1927</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Khoybun</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Xoybûn ('Independence') was a Kurdish nationalist league founded in 1927 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lebanon">Lebanon</a> by Kurdish exiles and intellectuals, including members of the Bedirkhan family. It organised and supported the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-ararat">Ararat</a> rebellion against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a> from 1927 to 1930, led in the field by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ihsan-nuri-pasha">Ihsan Nuri Pasha</a>. After the rebellion's defeat it continued mainly as a political and cultural movement among exiles in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> and Lebanon.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/xoybun.jpg" alt="Xoybûn" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Benohight214 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kurdish_flag_(Khoiboun).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>After the failure of the Sheikh Said rebellion of 1925, Kurdish nationalists founded the <b>Xoybun</b> league in 1927.</blockquote><a href="/state/republic-of-ararat">Republic of Ararat</a></li></ul></section>
